  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 213 PM EDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\nPleasant fall-like temperatures have been a welcome change to the \nheat of the previous weeks. For the next few days, we will maintain \na northerly flow through the column due to the strong low pressure \nsystem off the Mid-Atlantic/New England coastline and a ridge over \nthe Great Plains. Highs in the 70s and lows in the 40s to lower/mid \n50s will continue through the weekend. The pattern will favor dry \nweather as well, with abundant sunshine for most of the area. Some \nhigh cloud on the fringes of the Nor'easter could reach our northern \nsections by Monday, with no real impact. \n\nAs the ridge to our west shifts east and flattens out, a \ndeveloping southerly flow will bring warmer temperatures next week, \nwith highs in the 80s for most of the TN Valley by Tuesday. These \nabove normal temperatures will continue for most of next week. Late \nin the week, we may see some rain chances returning as a shortwave \ntrough may move into the Plains and MS Valley region.",
